FlashInfer commit b072eaac (Python package 0.6.15) crashes during NVFP4
CUTLASS MoE autotuning on SM121:

RuntimeError: [TensorRT-LLM][ERROR] Assertion failed:
quant_1 && quant_2 && quant_3 && quant_4 && quant_5 && quant_6
(cutlass_fused_moe_kernels.cuh:5034)

The regression appears to come from PR #3738 / merge commit 5823159c.

`GemmProfilerBackend::getProfilerWorkspaces()` previously allocated the six
FP4 profiler workspaces whenever the weight dtype was FP4. PR #3738 changed
that allocation guard to `isNativeWfp4Afp8Family()`, which requires FP8
activations.

Native NVFP4 uses FP4 activations and FP4 weights (`kFP4`, or `kINT64`
aliases), so the guard is false and all six workspace pointers remain null.
`prepareQuantParams()` still has an FP4×FP4 branch that requires all six
pointers, causing the assertion during GEMM1 autotuning.

Last known good FlashInfer commit: 517cca9c.

Suggested fix: include the native SM100+ FP4-activation × FP4-weight family in
the existing native FP4 workspace allocation branch. An NVFP4 test running
inside `autotune(True)` would cover this path.

